    "text": "## sub_530840_00530840 — Huffman sample render to word buffer\n\n**Summary:** Renders Huffman-decoded audio samples into 16-bit word output buffer. Reads codebook selectors, Huffman-decodes VQ indices from bitstream, applies scale table (a2) and index offsets (a5), writes 3 interleaved output words per iteration. Zero-fills unused output slots based on subband count and stereo flag.\n\n**Frame-path:** NOT_FOUND  \n**Call frequency:** UNKNOWN (no static path from tick root)\n\n**Called by:** TextureDecompression_1250 (00531250)\n\n**Struct fields accessed:**\n\n| Base | Offset | R/W | Init (literal → value) | Purpose |\n|------|--------|-----|------------------------|---------|\n| this | 0x24A4 | R | — | input bitstream buffer pointer (this[2345]) |\n| this | 0x24A8 | RW | — | bitstream bit-offset cursor (this[2346]), advances per Huffman read |\n| this | 0x24B8 | R | — | subband/granule count (this[2350]), loop bound |\n| this | 0x24CC | R | — | stereo flag / channel mode (this[2355]), ==2 for stereo |\n\n**Written-by note (persistence):**\n- this 0x24A8: updated per Huffman symbol read; cursor advances through input bitstream\n\n**Globals referenced:**\n\n| Address | Name | R/W | Role |\n|---------|------|-----|------|\n| 00531148 | jpt_530C9D | R | jump table for switch/case dispatch |\n| 005311c8 | jpt_530EF8 | R | jump table for switch/case dispatch |\n| 005b4788 | dword_5B4788 | R | HuffmanDecodeTable [DERIVED] |\n| 005da738 | dword_5DA738 | R | AnimationWeightScale [DERIVED] — scale factor offset table for Huffman decode |\n\n**Functions called:**\n\n| Address | Name | Purpose |\n|---------|------|---------|\n\n**Guard conditions (deterministic — field vs literal):**\n\n| Base | Offset | Test | Value | Field / meaning |\n|------|--------|------|-------|-----------------|\n| this | 0x24B8 | > | 0 | subband count (this[2350]) |\n| this | 0x24CC | != | 2 | stereo flag (this[2355]) |\n\n**Guard interpretation:** Entire decode loop skipped when this[2350] <= 0. When this[2355] != 2, the second-channel branch (lines processing a3[1], v9[32], v9[96]) is skipped — only mono output written. When this[2355] == 2, both left and right channel outputs are rendered. After loops, zero-fill switch runs to clear unused output slots up to index 159, with second switch block (indices 160-191) conditional on this[2355] == 2.\n"
